{"text": "ELIZABETH C. SAENZ, M.Ed.\n\nEDUCATION\n\nBIOGRAPHY\n\nElizabeth C. Saenz, a public-school trailblazer with experience spanning for over two\ndecades, is one of a few leaders to bridge the silos of leadership, management, and\ninnovation.\n\nStarting out as an educator back in 1990, Ms. Saenz has methodically built a strong and\ndiverse portfolio that includes twenty years as an administrator across four different\ndistricts.\n\nAcademically, her schools consistently \u201cMet Standard\u201d and earned several distinctions.\nOn the finance side, her leadership ensured the successful passages of bond elections,\nTRE\u2019s, and budgets that were aligned to identified campus and district goals.\n\nIt is clear Ms. Elizabeth Saenz\u2019s skill set is acutely attuned to the changing dynamics of\nigher accountability metrics and a complex school finance system. For many educators\n\nand students across Texas, she\u2019s in the category of one of the great leaders in education.\nSUMMARY OF PROFESSIONAL WORK HISTORY\ningage2Learn CDS, Trainer, Facilitator, & Coach 2016 - Present\nWest Oso ISD Superintendent 2011 \u2014 2016\nCotulla ISD Superintendent 2005 - 2011\nTASA Exec. Asst. for Special Projects 2003 - 2005\n3almorhea ISD Superintendent 2000 - 2003\nresidio ISD Bilingual Director 1998 \u2014 2000\n>residio ISD Campus Administrator 1996 \u2014 1998\n>residio ISD Professional Educator 1990 - 1996\n\nfre\n\nSUMMARY OF ACCOMPLISHMENTS\n\nCoached various Districts into building high performing cultures for student success and\nbecoming future-ready schools\nDistrict and all campuses have \u201cMet Standard\u201d since 2013 and received gold designations\nReceived Superior Achievement in FIRST Rating by TEA\nAwarded 21st Century Afterschool Centers for Education (ACE) Grant ($5.2M)\nIncreased the number of students successfully meeting TSI requirements and completing\nDual Credit courses at a negotiated reduced cost of $99 per course\nSuccessfully passed a Tax Ratification Election (TRE) with 82% voter support\n\nEDUCATION\n\nUniversity of Texas \u2014\nAustin\nCourse Completion Ed.D\nEducational\nAdministration\n(2005)\n\nSul Ross University\nMaster\u2019s in Education \u2014\nSchool Administration\n(1997)\n\nSul Ross University\nBachelor of Arts\nMajor: English\nMinor: Spanish\n(19)\n\nCERTIFICATIONS\n\nSuperintendent (PK-12)\nMid-Management (PK-12)\nEnglish (6-12)\n\nSpanish (6-12)",
